.SH NAME
.PP
auto-nfs-add-share - Add a directory to NFS exports

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-nfs-add-share directory clients [optional flags]
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
directory   Directory to export
clients     Network spec for allowed clients
flags       Additional NFS flags to add to the export entry
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-nfs-add-share
command exports "directory" as an NFS share and reloads the NFS
configuration.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-nfs-add-share /usr/home -network=192.168.0.0/24 -maproot=root
auto-nfs-add-share /usr/home '-network=192.168.0.0 255.255.255.0'
auto-nfs-add-share /share1 'bobspc.local julie.laptop.local'
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8), auto-nfs-restart(8)

